  "description": "<p>The <strong>n-queens</strong> puzzle is the problem of placing <code>n</code> queens on an <code>n x n</code> chessboard such that no two queens attack each other.</p>\n\n<p>Given an integer <code>n</code>, return <em>the number of distinct solutions to the&nbsp;<strong>n-queens puzzle</strong></em>.</p>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 1:</strong></p>\n<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets/problem_images/885d96b204b5968fcf9d0603991841065ac8e992af7659616ec7befca80fad08.jpg\" style=\"width: 600px; height: 268px;\" />\n<pre>\n<strong>Input:</strong> n = 4\n<strong>Output:</strong> 2\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> There are two distinct solutions to the 4-queens puzzle as shown.\n</pre>\n\n<p><strong class=\"example\">Example 2:</strong></p>\n\n<pre>\n<strong>Input:</strong> n = 1\n<strong>Output:</strong> 1\n</pre>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><code>1 &lt;= n &lt;= 9</code></li>\n</ul>\n",
  "task": "Solve the 'N-Queens II' problem on LeetCode.",
  "inputFormat": "Passed directly as parameters.",
  "outputFormat": "Returned value from the solution method.",
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= n <= 9"
  ],
